      "title": "extcap: Prevent some leaks in error cases",
      "message": "extcap: Prevent some leaks in error cases\n\nInstead of having a special free function that only frees the type of\nextcap_interface that we know we don't plan to steal, set the list\ndata to NULL when stealing the extcap_interface and call the ordinary\nfreeing function that does nothing on NULL. Also call the proper\nfunction in another error case.\n\nSeparately, if we want to know if there's already an executable assigned\nto an interface name before assigning it, use the lookup function\ninstead of generating a list of keys from before we starting parsing\nthe interfaces. Then we don't have to free that list of keys.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2026-08-29T10:41:08.000-04:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
